=\dfrac{\sin 65^{\circ}}{\cos 65^{\circ}}-2 \cdot \dfrac{\sin 40^{\circ}}{\cos 40^{\circ}}
=\dfrac{\sin 65^{\circ} \cos 40^{\circ}-2 \sin 40^{\circ} \cos 65^{\circ}}{\cos 65^{\circ} \cos 40^{\circ}}
=\dfrac{\sin (65^{\circ}-40^{\circ})}{\cos 65^{\circ} \cos 40^{\circ}}
=\dfrac{\sin 25^{\circ}(\cos 40^{\circ}-\sin 40^{\circ})}{\cos 65^{\circ} \cos 40^{\circ}}
=\dfrac{\sqrt{2} \sin 25^{\circ}(\cos 40^{\circ}-\sin 40^{\circ})}{2 \cos 65^{\circ} \cos 40^{\circ}}
=\dfrac{\sqrt{2} \sin 25^{\circ}(\cos 40^{\circ}-\sin 40^{\circ})}{2 \sin 25^{\circ} \cos 40^{\circ}}
=\dfrac{\sqrt{2}(\cos 40^{\circ}-\sin 40^{\circ})}{2\cos 40^{\circ}}_{\times \dfrac{\cos 40^{\circ}-\sin 40^{\circ}}{\cos 40^{\circ}-\sin 40^{\circ}}}=\sqrt{2}-1
\\\arctan (\tan 65^{\circ}-2 \tan 40^{\circ})=\arctan (\sqrt{2}-1)\in (0^{\circ}, 180^{\circ}) \implies\sqrt{x^2+1}=\dfrac{\sin 40^{\circ}}{\cos 40^{\circ}-\sin 40^{\circ}}
